    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The authors use a modified GPT-2 architecture to train models on binary data generated by ECAs. The model is trained to predict the next state of the automaton, given the current state. The training process involves pretraining the model on next-token prediction tasks, followed by fine-tuning on downstream tasks such as reasoning and chess move prediction. <strong>Attention patterns</strong> are analyzed to understand how the model integrates information from past states to make predictions.",
