      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "The authors find that models trained on more complex data exhibit greater predictive ability and perform better on downstream tasks. The results show a positive correlation between the complexity of the data and the model's performance, with a 'sweet spot' of complexity that is conducive to intelligence. <strong>Chaotic systems</strong> are found to be too random to predict, leading to poorer downstream performance.",
