    {
      "title": "Why It Matters",
      "content": "The findings of this study have implications for our understanding of intelligence in artificial systems and the importance of complexity in developing these systems. The results suggest that <strong>intelligence arises from the ability to predict complexity</strong>, and that creating intelligence may require only exposure to complexity. This has implications for the development of more advanced artificial intelligence systems and our understanding of human intelligence.",
